my-cv (cv) — "CV as code": tooling + personal CV content
========================================================

Copyright (c) 2026 Chu Chieu Du An (An Chu / Peter). All rights reserved.

This repository is a real, working CV. It falls into two clearly separated
parts, and they do NOT share the same licence. Read the part that applies to
what you want to take.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A. TOOLING — MIT Licence: copy it, change it, use it for your own CV
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Applies to: scripts/ (*.py, *.ps1), .github/workflows/*, Makefile, build.ps1,
templates/index.html, web/style.css, .editorconfig, .gitattributes, .gitignore,
and the "how it works" documentation in README.md.

See "Use this for your own CV" in README.md for a step-by-step.

